# HELP my_host_stops Boots of the window of the host (loop.window_boots) that ended in a stop, by cause: memory (an uncorrected memory error is on record in the boot), hardware-other (a fatal hardware error without one), panic (a panic with no hardware error record).
# TYPE my_host_stops gauge
my_host_stops{host="synth-crash-loop",cause="hardware-other"} 0
my_host_stops{host="synth-crash-loop",cause="memory"} 4
my_host_stops{host="synth-crash-loop",cause="panic"} 0
# HELP my_host_stop_streak The latest boots of the host in a row that a fatal hardware error ended; a boot still running is passed over.
# TYPE my_host_stop_streak gauge
my_host_stop_streak{host="synth-crash-loop"} 0
# HELP my_source_grade Best observation grade of the error records a source gave in the latest scan: 3 A (bank, row, column), 2 B (address or rank), 1 C (counts), 0 no error records. status says how reading the source went.
# TYPE my_source_grade gauge
my_source_grade{host="synth-crash-loop",source="synth",status="ok"} 3
